[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:28. No Parking]
[00:00.100]Passage 28 | 第28篇
[00:02.125]No parking. | 禁止停车。
[00:05.270]Jasper White is one of those rare people who believes in ancient myths. | 贾斯珀·怀特是那种相信古代神话的罕见人物之一。
[00:12.565]He has just bought a new house in the city, | 他刚在城里买了新房，
[00:16.000]but ever since he moved in, | 但自从他搬进来后，
[00:18.405]he has had trouble with motorists. | 他就一直被驾车者困扰。
[00:21.940]When he returns home at night, | 他每晚回家时，
[00:24.820]he always finds that someone has parked a car outside his gate. | 总是发现有人把车停在他家门口。
[00:30.770]Because of this, | 因此，
[00:32.810]he has not been able to get his own car into his garage even once. | 他一次都未能将自己的车开进车库。
[00:39.395]Jasper has put up no parking signs outside his gate, | 贾斯珀在他家门口竖起了禁止停车的牌子，
[00:44.485]but these have not had any effect. | 但这些牌子丝毫没有作用。
[00:47.645]Now, he has put an ugly stone head over the gate. | 现在，他在大门上方放了一个丑陋的石头人头。
[00:53.045]It is one of the ugliest faces I have ever seen. | 那是我见过最丑陋的面孔之一。
[00:57.800]I asked him what it was, | 我问他那是什么，
[01:00.420]and he told me that it was Medusa, the Gorgon. | 他告诉我那是美杜莎，那个戈尔贡。
[01:04.835]Jasper hopes that she will turn motorists to stone. | 贾斯珀希望她能把驾车者变成石头。
[01:09.635]But none of them has been turned to stone yet. | 但目前还没有人被变成石头。